 `certificates/n-1489.cert` | `9d2dee39333c34f335c0ff1f625bb9c3cc8c3ccdd3dbc4b3c86ce0d75d58aad7` |\n| **1568** | `certificates/n-1568.cert` | `be6fc60ea9ab46a62780cb1b35882cbbda9dc159b7ccf99a5970076f55387c86` |\n\n**Certificate.** 122 exact rational certificates in Evan Daniel's standard half-angle certificate format (`.cert`):\n- Repository: [Mishapolk/square-packing-records](https://github.com/Mishapolk/square-packing-records)\n- Pinned revision: [`12fc46678fa8eefa3f156ff37dfffd84c8f3a580`](https://github.com/Mishapolk/square-packing-records/tree/12fc46678fa8eefa3f156ff37dfffd84c8f3a580) (branch `main`)\n- Directory: [`certificates/`](https://github.com/Mishapolk/square-packing-records/tree/12fc46678fa8eefa3f156ff37dfffd84c8f3a580/certificates)\n\nEach certificate file `certificates/<filename>` specifies the count n, the exact rational side fraction S, and for each square the exact rational centre coordinates (x, y) and half-angle rotation parameter t = tan(theta/2). All coordinates and side lengths are represented as exact fractions of arbitrary-precision integers (p/q).\n\nEvery certificate has strictly positive wall clearance and strictly positive separating axis gaps, satisfying both open-container and closed-container non-overlap conditions with zero tolerance.\n\n**Checking.** Each certificate has been independently dual-checked with zero tolerance across independent verification engines:\n1. `tools/competitors/evand/search/exact/verify_cert.py` (Evan Daniel exact rational separating hyperplane & container containment verifier): **122 / 122 passed (100% strictly positive clearance)**\n2. `tools/jlevy_squares/packing/src/sqpack/verify.py` (Joshua Levy reference SQPACK verifier): **122 / 122 passed (100% exit code 0, zero mutual overlap)**\n\nCommands to rerun verification:\n```bash\npython3 tools/competitors/evand/search/exact/verify_cert.py scratch/square-packing-records/certificates/n*.cert\npython3 tools/jlevy_squares/packing/src/sqpack/verify.py scratch/square-packing-records/certificates/n*.cert\n```\n\n**What the checkers share.** `verify_cert.py` checks exact rational separating axes and wall containment. `sqpack/verify.py` is Joshua Levy's independent implementation. Both open-container margin conditions and closed-container non-overlap conditions are simultaneously satisfied with zero tolerance.\n\n**Not done.** No claim of global optimality is made. No local rigidity or Karush–Kuhn–Tucker (KKT) second-order optimality is claimed for the perturbed rational witnesses. These establish constructive upper bounds on s(N).\n\n**Lineage and credit.** Credit: Mishapolk (Mikhail Polk).\nThese packings build upon and refine foundational packings and discoveries by Erich Friedman, Joshua Levy, Evan Daniel, Francisco Couzo, Nate Chaoweeraprasit, Robert Barnett, Daniil Ostashev, Frits Goebel, Joost de Winter, and other contributors to the square packing record.\n\n**AI assistance.** Gemini assisted with solver scripting, precision checks, and formatting.\n", "comments": [], "createdAt": "2026-10-22T05:30:47Z", "labels": [{"color": "9EF70A", "description": "Tracking intake (saving, validation, tabulation, credits) of new results", "id": "LA_kwDOTXp6xc8AAAAC7ozsEw", "name": "intake"}], "number": 719, "title": "New packings: 122 verified upper bounds for square packing (N in [105, 1568]): registration request", "updatedAt": "2026-10-22T06:11:30Z", "url": "https://github.com/jlevy/squares/issues/719"}
